<title>USA: Tomkins says gets HSR termination on Stant.</title>
<headline>Tomkins says gets HSR termination on Stant.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tomkins PLC said Tuesday its previously announced offer buy Stant Corp has been granted early termination of the waiting period under the Hart- Scott-Rodino Antitrust Improvements Act.</p>
<p>A company spokeswoman said this means there are no antitrust issues involving its proposed purchase of Stant, and that it can go forward with the deal.</p>
<p>The company said Tomkins' wholly owned subsidiary, E&amp;W Acquisition Corp, has a pending cash tender offer to purchase all Stant's outstanding shares for $21.50 per share.</p>
<p>The company said its offer closes on May 8 and it expects to assume control of Stant shortly after that date.</p>
</text>
